        text: 'Your father\'s friend at the bank has given you a stool, a ledger and a salary of a hundred a year. The work is copying figures from one book into another under a gas mantle. At noon the clerks eat chops at a chop house in Change Alley and talk of South African gold shares. Your mother writes that you are wasted. You are inclined to agree.',
        basis: 'Invented. A plausible City opening for a younger son of the period; Lord Randolph Churchill did bank with the Rothschilds.',
